lisa-design:
- Nested ci-common is called as `./.github/workflows/ci-common.yml`: GitHub resolves a local ref in a called workflow to the repo + commit of the calling workflow file (this repo), per docs "from the same commit as the caller workflow" and act#1875 (works on GitHub, not in act). No workflows-ref input needed. Unproven until the mock caller PRs run.
- Shared lint configs (.golangci.yml, .regal/config.yaml) are fetched with actions/checkout from job.workflow_repository @ job.workflow_sha (contexts now documented on github.com), sparse, then moved to $RUNNER_TEMP and the clone deleted. Chosen over a workflows-ref input (notify-failure's approach; the base note "no job.workflow_sha context" is outdated). actionlint v1.7.12 doesn't know job.workflow_*; .github/actionlint.yaml silences exactly that message. An empty job.workflow_sha fails the lint job with an explicit error rather than silently checking out the caller repo.
- Shared configs apply only when the caller has none (.golangci.{yml,yaml,toml,json}; .regal/config.yaml or .regal.yaml). golangci base sets run.relative-path-mode: gomod because the file is read from outside the repo.
- Shared Regal config: ignores CCF layout rules (directory-package-mismatch, test-outside-test-package, no-defined-entrypoint, line-length, opa-fmt which the opa job checks with the pinned OPA) and downgrades idiomatic/performance/style to warnings; bugs/imports/testing stay errors. Without it, Regal defaults fail mock-plugin-policies-1 (spec: must pass) and every product policy repo. Product repos still have bugs/imports errors (e.g. imports/unresolved-reference) for their adoption PRs.
- lint-new-from-merge-base (default true): PR -> --new-from-merge-base=origin/<base_ref> (checkout fetch-depth 0); push -> --new-from-rev=<event.before> when that commit exists; otherwise lint everything.
- goreleaser check exit 2 (valid but deprecated properties) is a warning, exit 1 fails: plugin-template's archives.format is deprecated, so a strict check would fail mock-plugin-1 and every plugin copied from the template.
- go mod tidy check is `go mod tidy` + `git status --porcelain -- go.mod go.sum` (not `go mod tidy -diff`, which needs Go >= 1.23 in the caller's go.mod).
- required: needs every job, if: always(), fails on any result != success (none of the top-level jobs is conditional, so skipped also fails). ci-common's pull_request-only jobs are inside `common`, which still succeeds when they skip.
- Check steps after setup use `if: !cancelled() && steps.setup.outcome == 'success'` so one run reports every failing check.
- Tool pins: golangci-lint v2.11.4 (spec), GoReleaser v2.18.2, OPA 1.14.1 (input), Regal 0.43.0 (input). Jobs split as golangci-lint / go / goreleaser and opa / regal for parallelism and clear status names.
